Now let me look at the `vertexToLatLng` function more carefully. The issue is a "Use-of-uninitialized-value" found by MSAN. Let me look at the `_faceIjkPentToCellBoundary` function - specifically, when `start` is not 0, the `lastFijk` variable is used before being initialized. Let me check:

In `_faceIjkPentToCellBoundary`:
```c
g->numVerts = 0;
FaceIJK lastFijk;  // <-- uninitialized!
for (int vert = start; vert < start + length + additionalIteration; vert++) {
    int v = vert % NUM_PENT_VERTS;
    FaceIJK fijk = fijkVerts[v];
    _adjustPentVertOverage(&fijk, adjRes);
    if (isResolutionClassIII(res) && vert > start) {
        // uses lastFijk here
        ...
    }
    ...
    lastFijk = fijk;
}
```

When `start > 0` and `vert == start`, the condition `vert > start` is false, so `lastFijk` isn't used on the first iteration. But wait, let me check `_adjustPentVertOverage`:

